<h2>Prerequisites</h2>
<ul>
    <li>You are <a href="../../login">logged in</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h1>How to enable Creator mode for your account</h1>
<h2>Activation</h2>
<p>The first step of enabling Creator mode, is activating Creator mode.<br>You can do so <a href="../../streamer/activate" target="_blank">here</a>.</p>
<img src="../../i/g/how_to_enable_creator_and_use_modules/img0.png" alt="activation screen">
<h2>Creator configuration</h2>
<p>After you have agreed to our terms and clicked 'enable' you will be greeted by our configuration screen. <br>Here you will be required to add a small and normal description for your account. <br>These can be seen your Creator page your viewers will use.</p>
<img src="../../i/g/how_to_enable_creator_and_use_modules/img1.png" alt="setup screen">
<p>After clicking 'done', you will be redirected to the Creator dashboard.</p>
<h1>How to setup your modules</h1>
<h2>How modules work</h2>
<p>Modules are different events that viewers can activate. Every module can be priced for however much you like.<br>To toggle a module, simply click on the slider at the bottom right of the module. <br>It is also a good idea to change the price so you can customize how often your viewers can activate it.<br>It is important to note that after editing a module, you need to click on 'save' to save your changes.<br>You can edit one module at a time, after clicking 'save' other changes will not be saved.</p>
<p>At the top of the page, there is a section that helps you set the correct price for your modules.<br>In this section, you will also find your token. This token should be kept private, and only used in official Streamer Options mods and plugins.<br>Only use this token when our official guides say so.</p>
<h4>You should now know how to activate your Creator account and how to set up modules.</h4>